  "adaptations": [
    "No source-owner paths, accounts, history, host settings, secrets, Git publication permissions or project-specific Endge policies.",
    "Memory consent and communication style belong to the new instance configuration.",
    "Managed module discovery uses verified copies; custom skill originals use registered links.",
    "Project note corrections retain old content in correction history instead of competing current entries.",
    "Installer lifecycle retains receipts and legacy card compatibility; live global Jarvis is not reinstalled.",
    "Long work retains rule IDs and role/permission boundaries; unsupported context-cost assertions are omitted.",
    "Engineering experiment budgets have one normative owner; experiments provides execution procedure.",
    "Automations port task/state ownership and executor boundaries, without copying active tasks or schedules.",
    "Writing examples retain teaching content without importing the original owner style preferences.",
    "Resource access retains resource-based selection and permission boundaries, using the new owner's ignored local/secrets or OS credential manager; no source access vault or standing synchronization rights are copied."
  ],
  "source_snapshot": "Observed working-tree file hashes; source_commit identifies HEAD, not a claim that the source tree is clean."
